[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1646799568","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1646799568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1646799568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iKCrQ","user":{"login":"changeset-bot[bot]","id":49419645,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk0MTk2NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/28616?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/changeset-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/changeset-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-23T10:05:57Z","updated_at":"2023-08-29T07:52:12Z","body":"###  ⚠️  No Changeset found\n\nLatest commit: c23740305943f7db26dff24786189f027c59310a\n\nMerging this PR will not cause a version bump for any packages. If these changes should not result in a new version, you're good to go. **If these changes should result in a version bump, you need to add a changeset.**\n\n\n\n[Click here to learn what changesets are, and how to add one](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/adding-a-changeset.md).\n\n[Click here if you're a maintainer who wants to add a changeset to this PR](https://github.com/y-nk/astro/new/main?filename=.changeset/lucky-news-bow.md&value=---%0A%22%40fake-scope%2Ffake-pkg%22%3A%20patch%0A---%0A%0Afeat%3A%20implement%20partial%20build%0A)\n\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1646799568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1647815521","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1647815521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1647815521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iN6th","user":{"login":"ematipico","id":602478,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjQ3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/602478?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico","html_url":"https://github.com/ematipico","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-24T12:25:53Z","updated_at":"2023-07-24T12:26:27Z","body":"@y-nk Thank you for proposing this feature. A few things that I am missing; could you please address them?\r\n\r\n1. The function seems to be applied only when we **generate** the page, although we build it anyway. Should we also **not build** it? It would make the whole build faster;\r\n2. I believe the filtering should be applied [here](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/main/packages/astro/src/core/build/generate.ts#L141-L181). Doing so, we avoid **importing** the page to generate. What do you think?\r\n3. What about SSR? Is this feature meant also for SSR? ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1647815521/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1647910240","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1647910240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1647910240,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iOR1g","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-24T13:28:05Z","updated_at":"2023-07-24T13:28:05Z","body":"@ematipico thanks for your time spent on reviewing this.\n\n1. I'm honestly lost at the generate/build nuance. i'm not sure to have enough knowledge to understand this.\n\n2. i first thought on putting the filtering where you pointed, but it does not expand the filtering to paths generated from `getStaticPaths` (with dynamic params in it). For this to happen it needs to be within `generatePage`. i'm thinking we could also add the \"raw\" path - containing the params - too and decide to skip import it if the function returned false (like a grouped filter, if you follow me)\n\n3. the feature is definitely not meant for SSR, that's why i put the config in `build` rather than root level. it is intended for build only, and for filtering pre-renderable (prerender=true) route paths only (writing this i realize that api routes are not - yet - covered here)\n\nThe usecase addressed is to skip pages which should not be built, defined by a criteria in userland. this might not make sense when using content collection, but it does when using a 3rd party CMS (but one could still use the output of a git diff of `src/content` maybe?)\n\nApplied to my current usecase, my project has `src/pages/[...path].astro` where all route paths are pulled from a strapi backend and generated at built. i want to wire strapi's webhook to my build github action so that only updated pages get rebuilt and deployed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1647910240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648107688","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1648107688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1648107688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iPCCo","user":{"login":"lilnasy","id":69170106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MTcwMTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69170106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy","html_url":"https://github.com/lilnasy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilnasy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-24T15:13:50Z","updated_at":"2023-07-24T15:13:50Z","body":"@y-nk  Regarding your first point,  the two processes can be thought of as compiling, and rendering (to HTML). From looking at the PR, I can tell it prevents some pages from being rendered, but we still pay the cost of `.astro` to `.ts` compilation, css and js compilation and optimizations for the entire project, etc. In effect, this PR is like SSR + prerendering but only the prerendered pages are kept and no server runtime is created.\n\nRegarding the third point, the `build` section of the astro config has implications on both server and static _builds_. A more appropriate place might be output (`\"output\": \"static-partial\"`). It sounds drastic but that's the category of change this PR implies.\n\nI would look into how this change could be made into an integration. And if that's not possible, what could we change in the Integrations API to make it possible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648107688/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648829583","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1648829583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1648829583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iRySP","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T01:25:05Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T15:10:12Z","body":"@lilnasy i've tried to make this an integration prior making the change here, and followed @natemoo-re advice (given in discord) that making a PR in astro would be a better option given what i wanted to achieve.\r\n\r\nAbout the \"cost of ts\" i do agree and this is on point... but there's sadly no way to make it not happening otherwise since there's no function encapsulation in astro components: we have to import the file to execute `getStaticPaths` and get the generated routes.\r\n\r\n~For the part of cost of css etc, I didn't check on this - it was my expectation that skipping a page in `generatePage` that early would result in the rest of the process being trimmed out as well.~ \r\n\r\nedit: i think i made a commit which solves that.\r\n\r\ni will add an earlier filtering for pages which don't have dynamic params so that the process can be optimized to its maximum. \r\n\r\nedit: done 👌 \r\n\r\nI agree with you that it's conceptually a `output: static-partial` but i think it's not a right way to go. it'd be clearly a bad DX since the goal of this feature is to be able to produce a partial static build _to be used in ci_. People using this would end up switching the `output` between `static-partial` and `static` or `hybrid` and have to deal with a different shape of `dist/` all the time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648829583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648866380","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1648866380","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1648866380,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iR7RM","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T02:08:26Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T07:50:48Z","body":"to bring a bit of light on this further, the project i'm testing this on has ~1000 pages (~100x10 locales) pulled from a distant strapi backend.\r\n\r\nthe full build with `output: \"hybrid\"` is ~5mn (i also have further optimizations to help speed up the build process such as cached/deduped fetch calls)\r\n\r\nwhen i add `filterPage: (path) => path.startsWith(\"/fr/\")` in my astro.config, i get only the expected pages built and the whole process happens in under 1mn.\r\n\r\nwhat i mean is that even tho we may pay the cost of js/css, the performances are still quite much better than a full build and the output is as expected ; at least from what I'm testing... could you propose some cases which would help me tackle corner cases?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1648866380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1649400415","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1649400415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1649400415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iT9pf","user":{"login":"ematipico","id":602478,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjQ3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/602478?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico","html_url":"https://github.com/ematipico","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ematipico/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T08:49:13Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T08:49:33Z","body":"> @ematipico thanks for your time spent on reviewing this.\r\n> \r\n>     1. I'm honestly lost at the generate/build nuance. i'm not sure to have enough knowledge to understand this.\r\n> \r\n\r\nWe can prevent bundling a page easily, that's where you can write your code. `pageData` has everything you need\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/25e04a2ecbda7952a68220ce6739ae1c75144858/packages/astro/src/core/build/plugins/plugin-pages.ts#L45-L47\r\n\r\n>     2. i first thought on putting the filtering where you pointed, but it does not expand the filtering to paths generated from `getStaticPaths` (with dynamic params in it). For this to happen it needs to be within `generatePage`. i'm thinking we could also add the \"raw\" path - containing the params - too and decide to skip import it if the function returned false (like a grouped filter, if you follow me)\r\n> \r\n\r\nOh, so your feature needs to work on the final URL? It wasn't very clear from your description. Then we should not called `pagePath` but `pageURL`, or `generatedPageUrl`. Maybe we should update the description to highlight the fact that the feature is meant to filter generated pages after the execution of `getStaticPaths`. It's really important.\r\n\r\nGiven this, I suppose my first point doesn't apply anymore.\r\n\r\n>     3. the feature is definitely not meant for SSR, that's why i put the config in `build` rather than root level. it is intended for build only, and for filtering pre-renderable (prerender=true) route paths only (writing this i realize that api routes are not - yet - covered here)\r\n> \r\n\r\nThat's definitely another aspect of your proposed feature that should be highlighted in the description.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1649400415/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1649595443","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1649595443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1649595443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iUtQz","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T10:44:04Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T11:51:46Z","body":"@ematipico Thanks for your feedback. I'll proceed with the renaming of `pagePath` to be `pageURL`. You're right that it's more proper. Also I'll update the description of the PR accordingly, i _think_ you're right and most people reviewing got the wrong idea due to a bad description.\r\n\r\nEDIT: done 👌 \r\n\r\nYour 1st point still apply for pages with `prerender=true` which don't have `getStaticPaths`. I've added code in that regard, but due to how soon it is implemented in the build i'm clueless how to make this \"skipped\" information pop in the build log.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1649595443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651170778","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651170778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651170778,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iat3a","user":{"login":"bluwy","id":34116392,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MTE2Mzky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34116392?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy","html_url":"https://github.com/bluwy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T07:54:10Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T07:54:10Z","body":"From a brief look, I think this would be a nice feature as experimental for now. I think it's safer too to only skip on generation rather than build since we're tracking inter-page information during build, and skipping some might affect the final chunk names that otherwise the filtered pages would wrongly use.\r\n\r\nThe docs should probably mention that it only works for static builds though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651170778/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651176048","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651176048","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651176048,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iavJw","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T07:57:55Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T07:57:55Z","body":"@bluwy hello and thanks for your time spent on the review.\r\n\r\n1. as i understand you would rather remove the code added in `page-data`?\r\n2. i'll try to update the docs again!\r\n3. i'm not sure on how to create an \"experimental feature\"; could you briefly (bullet-point style) explain to me the big steps? from there i'm sure i can pick it up.\r\n\r\n🙏\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651176048/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651208498","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651208498","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651208498,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85ia3Ey","user":{"login":"bluwy","id":34116392,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MTE2Mzky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34116392?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy","html_url":"https://github.com/bluwy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T08:20:14Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T08:20:14Z","body":"> 1. as i understand you would rather remove the code added in `page-data`?\r\n\r\nI _think_ so. In your case with CMSes, they likely won't import any of your local style or scripts so you'd less likely see the issue (?). But for those who specifically wanted to build certain pages only, they might see the inconsistency. We currently have [this logic](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/db8c04002f51e89df57d44680e9e562105505aa4/packages/astro/src/core/build/plugins/plugin-css.ts#L78-L104) to determine what name to give a CSS chunk deriving from pages, and having missing pages could cause different names to appear.\r\n\r\n> 3\\. i'm not sure on how to create an \"experimental feature\"; could you briefly (bullet-point style) explain to me the big steps? from there i'm sure i can pick it up.\r\n\r\nMaking it experimental is probably my opinion/instinct for now as I feel like ultimately we could have a better implementation like ISR? So optional unless another maintainer chimes in, but to acheive that:\r\n\r\n1. It would be very similar changes you did in `schema.ts`, but to the `experimental:` field, e.g. [here](https://github.com/withastro/astro/blob/db8c04002f51e89df57d44680e9e562105505aa4/packages/astro/src/core/config/schema.ts#L233-L240).\r\n2. Then it's mostly changing `build.filterPages` to `experimental.buildPages`. We did this similarly for `inlineStylesheets`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThanks for keeping up on the PR!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651208498/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651226878","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651226878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651226878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85ia7j-","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T08:32:35Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T08:33:49Z","body":"@bluwy thanks a lot i will apply moving to `experimental` today at most.\r\n\r\n> Making it experimental is probably my opinion/instinct for now as I feel like ultimately we could have a better implementation like ISR?\r\n\r\nOn this point i do not think this would be better/worse, as the goal of ISR is (i think) different.\r\n\r\nAs I understand it, ISR only works for _non statically-built_ pages and provides an \"in-memory/in-container\" cached build of the page (and serve it). here the goal is rather \"partial SSG\".\r\n\r\nWhat i'm planning on building after is similar to ISR _but does not require a running server_ as my plan is to wire my CMS's webhook to a CI runner and rebuild/deploy only a subset of updated pages.\r\n\r\nFor the goal of ISR, it's a bit more difficult as it involves touching the server part, but i would think that it's not harder than building a `const cachedPages: Map<URL, Response>` and shortcutting the rendering of a page based on some criterias.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651226878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651232040","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651232040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651232040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85ia80o","user":{"login":"bluwy","id":34116392,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MTE2Mzky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34116392?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy","html_url":"https://github.com/bluwy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluwy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T08:35:59Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T08:35:59Z","body":"Thanks I might have confused how ISR works, but what I had in mind is definitely in line with yours. I was thinking writing the build metadata somewhere and using it on the next run to identify which page needs to be re-generated.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651232040/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651750412","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1651750412","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1651750412,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85ic7YM","user":{"login":"ShivamJoker","id":23727670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNzI3Njcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23727670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker","html_url":"https://github.com/ShivamJoker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShivamJoker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T12:54:46Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T12:54:46Z","body":"I would love to have an option which generates the pages/paths which was updated.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1651750412/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1652138384","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1652138384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1652138384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85ieaGQ","user":{"login":"florian-lefebvre","id":69633530,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjMzNTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69633530?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre","html_url":"https://github.com/florian-lefebvre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/florian-lefebvre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T16:24:29Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T16:24:29Z","body":"I haven't read every single comment but I think it could make sense to also apply this for SSR pages. Here is my usecase:\r\n\r\nI'm using [Keystatic](https://keystatic.com/) and following [their guide](https://keystatic.com/docs/installation-astro#astro-s-ssr-hybrid-mode) we make this page ssr + client only.\r\nHowever, because I'm using [local strategy](https://keystatic.com/docs/local-vs-git-hub-storage-strategy#local-strategy), it only makes sense to keep it in dev mode.\r\n\r\nSo this PR is a great start, but I think having a way to disable SSR pages as well would be great.\r\n\r\nAnother thought: I like the `export const prerender = boolean` api to opt out of prerendering. I think it could also make sense in this context with something like `export const exclude = boolean`. Other names could be: include, generate","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1652138384/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1656997393","html_url":"https://github.com/withastro/astro/pull/7769#issuecomment-1656997393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/7769","id":1656997393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFL76Q85iw8YR","user":{"login":"y-nk","id":411625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTYyNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk","html_url":"https://github.com/y-nk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y-nk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-30T02:12:43Z","updated_at":"2023-08-02T02:21:09Z","body":"@florian-lefebvre to be clear my goal is *not* to introduce a \"do not include this route in the build\" api. \r\n\r\nmy goal is to have static routes generated from dynamic params (with `getStaticPaths`, which could be 10000s) to avoid being all generated when only a subset needs to be regenerated.\r\n\r\nif you don't want a ssr route in the build, and ou can simply prefix with a `_` before you build your project. you can even automate this with a prebuild/postbuild npm script (`mv src/pages/my-ssr.astro src/pages/_my-ssr.astro` and back)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/withastro/astro/issues/comments/1656997393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https:/